    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Adoption of the RNS system is deepening within Level 4 epilepsy centers and extending into community settings, supporting steady momentum in the core adult focal epilepsy indication. The company is advancing an AI-enabled seizure identification tool and preparing a PMA supplement for idiopathic generalized epilepsy, signaling potential expansion into a broader patient population. Market sentiment is mixed: operational execution is solid, yet the stock’s post-earnings weakness and a recent 12-month high reflect tension between growth traction and investor impatience with sustained unprofitability.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is deliberately front-loading operating expenses to fund AI development and pipeline expansion, prioritizing long-term competitive positioning over near-term profitability. The team reiterated a full-year revenue outlook that implies continued growth while guiding for an adjusted EBITDA loss, a posture that shows confidence in the trajectory but also invites scrutiny on the timeline to breakeven. An earnings beat and transparent commentary provide moderate credibility, though mixed analyst ratings and a muted market response indicate lingering skepticism about the pace of conversion from topline gains to sustainable earnings.",
